Parent: 1544

## Context

Addition 2 of `design/2026-11-12-guichet-inter-repo-dialogue.md` § 5: a premise check at pickup. The trial (`design/research/2026-11-12-guichet-triage-trial.md`)
showed triage adds value only on reports that assert something checkable
and wrong (G2, H3), and harms when it refuses on recorded text the owner
then changes (G3, H1).

## Scope

- `/hunt` (Plan) and raid (Verify), on a ticket with a `filed from` line,
  start with the trial brief's four checks: facts against framing,
  duplicates and overlap, ownership, standing rulings.
- A conflict with a recorded ruling goes to the author as a question
  (`rules/workflow.md` § Escalation protocol), never as a refusal or a
  pushback.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Both skills run the four checks on foreign tickets and route a ruling
      conflict as a question.
- [x] Replayed on the trial's G2 and H3 reports, the check names the
      corrections the owners later made.
- [x] `make check` passes.
